<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- TemporalWindowActivityExpander — the bottom band of a temporal window: what Anvil is WORKING ON for THAT mode
     (TemporalActivityViewModel), in TWO states moved by ONE pull tab. Declared ONCE in TemporalWindow, under whichever
     Content is loaded. It replaced the main bar's activity slot (2026-10-16); three states became two (2026-10-19).

       …the Content's list, scrolling UNDER the band's edge…
       ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░     ← EDGE-SHADE (trial): the list DARKENS into
       ▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒╭─ ˄ More ─╮▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒     the band — the main bar's black fade made
       ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓│          │▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓     DENSER (DenseShadowFadeUp, solid at the
       ──────────────────────────┘          └───────────────────────     edge), STRAIGHT across, 36 px = the tab's
                                                                          26 px rise + 10 (the main bars match). The
                                                                          TAB laps the hairline 2 px.
     HIDDEN (ONE line, 2026-10-21 — the same height as ForeCast's, idle or busy):
       ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━  ← busy: the progress RIDES THE TOP EDGE (EdgeProgress, 2 px)
       Radar · next check 1:47:30 PM             Scan due ~1:47:12 PM  ●  ← busy: "New scan" | "1:47:12 PM scan ·
                                                                          painting"; ● = a feed failed (tooltip names it)
       ForeCast / PastCast Hidden (no radar line) = the summary line instead: "Outlooks current · last …"
     FULL (˅ Less) — idea A, one table:
       New scan                                1:47:12 PM scan · painting
       █████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░
       ─────────────────────────────────────────
         FEED                 EVERY        LAST          NEXT       ← fixed labels (TemporalWindowActivityExpanderFeedRow
       ● Radar                scan    1:42:51 PM    1:47:30 PM        IsHeader); each row LIFTS on hover
       ● Warnings             live   12:04:31 PM   when issued      ← feeds in the window's layer order; "live" =
       ● Storm cells          60 s   12:04:10 PM   12:05:10 PM        a live source carries it (LiveFeedChannel)
       ● Tropical             live   failed 12:00 PM when issued
       ─────────────────────────────────────────
       ● Live via IEM · connected since 11:02 AM    ← THE SOURCE LINE (NowCast; LiveDataViewModel): amber "IEM lost
                                                       at 12:08:31 PM · polling until it's back" while it's down

     The band is the RAISED tier face (OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedBrush) so the tab — Raised, the main rail's tabs' face —
     blends into it with no seam. Top hairline turns the TONE colour while the radar is loud (blue = working · green =
     done · red = failed). ForeCast: no radar line, ONE feed row (Outlooks) + the source line; Hidden = "Outlooks current ·
     last …".
     PASTCAST (2026-10-19, idea A): what the LOADED EVENT downloaded — no radar line, no feed table; its own table:
       KTLX · May 20, 2013 · 1:00 PM–3:00 PM                 loaded 3:12 PM   ← the gate's event line
       ─────────────────────────────────────────
         LAYER                RESULT                SOURCE       ← TemporalWindowActivityExpanderLoadRow (IsHeader)
       ● Radar                96 frames             NEXRAD (AWS)
       ● Damage surveys       failed 3:12 PM        [ Retry ]    ← PastLayerStatus rows, PastCast's layer order
       ● Tropical             none in window        IEM
       ─────────────────────────────────────────
       ● 8 of 9 layers loaded · Damage surveys failed   ← also the HIDDEN line (Activity.Summary)

     ⚠️ NOTHING COUNTS DOWN (the user's call, 2026-10-19): every time is a CLOCK time; only a busy scan's bar moves.
     ⚠️ TABULAR DIGITS on every number (TabularNumberTextStyle) + FIXED columns (the row control owns their widths).
     ⚠️ Reserved rows: within a state the band's height never changes as lines come and go (bars hide by Opacity).
     ⚠️ Text: 13.5 / 13 px lines, 11 px small-caps labels (was 12 / 11.5 — "a little bigger").
     ⚠️ The tone colours are LITERALS (code-behind), like the gate's: never resolve a theme brush in C#.
     ⚠️ Wording lives in the view models (BarActivityViewModel, FeedStatus, TemporalActivityViewModel), not here. -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.TemporalWindows.TemporalWindowActivityExpander"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:tw="using:Anvil.Controls.TemporalWindows"
             xmlns:ctl="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             xmlns:vm="using:Anvil.ViewModels"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d"
             IsTabStop="False">

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <!-- One FEED row (the row control owns the columns, the hover and the failed red). -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="FeedRowTemplate" x:DataType="vm:FeedStatus">
            <tw:TemporalWindowActivityExpanderFeedRow Status="{x:Bind}"/>
        </DataTemplate>
        <!-- One PastCast LAYER row (the row control owns the columns, the hover, the red and Retry). -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="LoadRowTemplate" x:DataType="vm:PastLayerStatus">
            <tw:TemporalWindowActivityExpanderLoadRow Status="{x:Bind}"/>
        </DataTemplate>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <Grid>
        <!-- THE BAND. -->
        <Grid x:Name="Band" Background="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedBrush}">
            <!-- The top hairline (themed), then THE TONE EDGE over it: code-behind sets its literal brush and fades its
                 opacity (ApplyTone) — a quiet tone fades it out WITHOUT changing the brush, so a green flash fades green.
                 Two elements, not a Border + child: a child can't paint over its parent's own border. -->
            <Border Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Top" IsHitTestVisible="False"
                    Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
            <Border x:Name="ToneEdge" Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Top" Opacity="0" IsHitTestVisible="False">
                <Border.OpacityTransition>
                    <ScalarTransition Duration="0:0:0.3"/>
                </Border.OpacityTransition>
            </Border>
            <!-- HIDDEN's busy bar (2026-10-21): the radar's progress RIDES THE TOP EDGE, so the Hidden band is one line
                 tall (ForeCast's height). Full keeps its bars under the radar line. Shown only while busy. -->
            <Grid x:Name="EdgeProgress" Height="2" VerticalAlignment="Top" IsHitTestVisible="False"
                  Visibility="{x:Bind ShownWhen(Activity.IsHidden, Activity.HasRadar), Mode=OneWay}"
                  Opacity="{x:Bind BusyOpacity(Activity.Radar.IsShown, Activity.Radar.HasProgress), Mode=OneWay}">
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="{x:Bind Filled(Activity.Radar.Progress), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="{x:Bind Rest(Activity.Radar.Progress), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <Border Background="{x:Bind ToneBrush(Activity.Radar.Tone), Mode=OneWay}"/>
            </Grid>

            <!-- 10 px sides + each row's own 6 = text on the window's 16 px edge. -->
            <StackPanel Margin="10,11,10,11">

                <!-- ===== THE RADAR LINE (both states): busy = the activity, idle = the next check (dimmed). ===== -->
                <StackPanel x:Name="RadarLine" Padding="6,0"
                            Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.HasRadar), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Opacity="{x:Bind LinesOpacity(Activity.Radar.IsShown), Mode=OneWay}">
                    <StackPanel.OpacityTransition>
                        <ScalarTransition Duration="0:0:0.25"/>
                    </StackPanel.OpacityTransition>
                    <Grid ColumnSpacing="8" Height="20">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/> <!-- HIDDEN: the failed-feed dot -->
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Activity.Radar.Title, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13.5"
                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       Style="{StaticResource TabularNumberTextStyle}"/>
                            <Border Padding="5,0" CornerRadius="4" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                    Background="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"
                                    Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(Activity.Radar.QueuedText), Mode=OneWay}">
                                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Activity.Radar.QueuedText, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="11" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                           Style="{StaticResource TabularNumberTextStyle}"
                                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextOnAccentFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                            </Border>
                        </StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{x:Bind Activity.Radar.Detail, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Center" Style="{StaticResource TabularNumberTextStyle}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                        <!-- HIDDEN only: the feed summary line is gone (one line, 2026-10-21), so a feed in trouble shows
                             as this red dot; its tooltip is the summary that names it. -->
                        <Ellipse Grid.Column="2" Width="8" Height="8" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="#FFF85149"
                                 Visibility="{x:Bind ShownWhen(Activity.IsHidden, Activity.SummaryHasFailure), Mode=OneWay}"
                                 ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind Activity.Summary, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- The busy bar + its thin download line: FULL only (Hidden's rides the top edge — EdgeProgress);
                         always laid out there, shown only while busy (no idle countdown fill — nothing counts down). -->
                    <Grid Height="4" CornerRadius="2" Margin="0,5,0,0"
                          Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.IsFull), Mode=OneWay}"
                          Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"
                          Opacity="{x:Bind BusyOpacity(Activity.Radar.IsShown, Activity.Radar.HasProgress), Mode=OneWay}">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="{x:Bind Filled(Activity.Radar.Progress), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="{x:Bind Rest(Activity.Radar.Progress), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Border CornerRadius="2" Background="{x:Bind ToneBrush(Activity.Radar.Tone), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    </Grid>
                    <Grid Height="2" CornerRadius="1" Margin="0,2,0,0"
                          Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.IsFull), Mode=OneWay}"
                          Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"
                          Opacity="{x:Bind BusyOpacity(Activity.Radar.IsShown, Activity.Radar.HasSecondary), Mode=OneWay}">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="{x:Bind Filled(Activity.Radar.Secondary), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="{x:Bind Rest(Activity.Radar.Secondary), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Border CornerRadius="1" Background="#FF8A8F98"/>
                    </Grid>
                </StackPanel>

                <!-- ===== HIDDEN without a radar line (ForeCast, PastCast): the one-line feed summary. NowCast's Hidden
                     is the radar line ALONE (one line, 2026-10-21) — a failed feed is its red dot. ===== -->
                <!-- No top margin: it never follows the radar line now, and 11 + 20 + 11 = the radar line's Hidden height. -->
                <StackPanel x:Name="FeedSummary" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="7" Height="20" Margin="6,0"
                            Visibility="{x:Bind SummaryShown(Activity.IsHidden, Activity.HasSummary, Activity.HasRadar), Mode=OneWay}">
                    <Ellipse Width="8" Height="8" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="#FFF85149"
                             Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.SummaryHasFailure), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Activity.Summary, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" Style="{StaticResource TabularNumberTextStyle}"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                </StackPanel>

                <!-- ===== FULL: the FEED table — labels, the radar's row, then every feed. ===== -->
                <StackPanel x:Name="FeedTable" Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.IsFull), Mode=OneWay}">
                    <StackPanel x:Name="FeedRows" Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.HasFeedTable), Mode=OneWay}">
                        <Border Height="1" Margin="6,10,6,4" Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                        <tw:TemporalWindowActivityExpanderFeedRow x:Name="TemporalWindowActivityExpanderFeedRowHeader" IsHeader="True"/>
                        <tw:TemporalWindowActivityExpanderFeedRow x:Name="TemporalWindowActivityExpanderFeedRowRadar"
                                                                  Status="{x:Bind Activity.Radar.Status, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                                  Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.HasRadar), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                        <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{x:Bind Activity.Feeds, Mode=OneWay}"
                                      ItemTemplate="{StaticResource FeedRowTemplate}"/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- PASTCAST's table (idea A, 2026-10-19): what the loaded event downloaded, layer by layer. -->
                    <StackPanel x:Name="PastTable" Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.HasPastLayers), Mode=OneWay}">
                        <Grid Height="22" Padding="6,0" ColumnSpacing="12">
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Activity.EventLine, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13.5" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" Style="{StaticResource TabularNumberTextStyle}"/>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{x:Bind Activity.LoadedText, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center" Style="{StaticResource TabularNumberTextStyle}"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                        </Grid>
                        <Border Height="1" Margin="6,6,6,4" Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                        <tw:TemporalWindowActivityExpanderLoadRow x:Name="TemporalWindowActivityExpanderLoadRowHeader" IsHeader="True"/>
                        <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{x:Bind Activity.PastLayers, Mode=OneWay}"
                                      ItemTemplate="{StaticResource LoadRowTemplate}"/>
                        <Border Height="1" Margin="6,6,6,4" Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="7" Height="22" Padding="6,0">
                            <Ellipse Width="8" Height="8" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="#FFF85149"
                                     Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.SummaryHasFailure), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Activity.Summary, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" Style="{StaticResource TabularNumberTextStyle}"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- THE SOURCE LINE (idea B, 2026-10-19): which live service the feeds' times come from, or why they
                         poll. Full state only; NowCast only (Activity.HasLive). Words: LiveDataViewModel.SourceLine. -->
                    <StackPanel x:Name="SourceLine" Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.HasLive), Mode=OneWay}">
                        <Border Height="1" Margin="6,6,6,4" Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="7" Height="22" Padding="6,0">
                            <Ellipse Width="8" Height="8" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                     Fill="{x:Bind LinkBrush(Activity.Live.LinkState), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Activity.Live.SourceLine, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" Style="{StaticResource TabularNumberTextStyle}"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </StackPanel>
                </StackPanel>
            </StackPanel>
        </Grid>

        <!-- ===== EDGE-SHADE (trial, 2026-10-19): the list DARKENS into the band as it slides under it — the main
             bar's black fade made DENSER (Styles.xaml DenseShadowFadeUp, solid black at the edge) — STRAIGHT across,
             36 deep = the tab's 26 px rise (its 28 less the 2 px lap) + 10, so the fade starts just above the tab and
             the tab stands in its dark part. The main bars' cast shadow is the same brush and depth (OverlayBar).
             It hangs OUTSIDE the band on a negative margin (Height = the margin, keep them equal), reserves no layout,
             never takes the pointer. Strength themed (OverlayBarShadowOpacity: 0.4 light, none in high contrast). -->
        <Border Height="36" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="0,-36,0,0" IsHitTestVisible="False"
                Background="{StaticResource DenseShadowFadeUp}"
                Opacity="{ThemeResource OverlayBarShadowOpacity}"/>
        <!-- ===== /EDGE-SHADE ===== -->

        <!-- THE TAB: the main rail's pull tab (Primitives/OverlayBarTab), Raised to wear the band's face, lapping the
             band's hairline 2 px (its own -2 foot margin; -26 here = its 28 less that lap). ManualToggle: a click
             Advances the state; IsShown is only the chevron (down = the click closes), Label the word. -->
        <ctl:OverlayBarTab x:Name="ActivityTab"
                           VerticalAlignment="Top" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,-26,0,0"
                           Raised="True" ManualToggle="True"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind Shown(Activity.HasContent), Mode=OneWay}"
                           IsShown="{x:Bind Not(Activity.OpensMore), Mode=OneWay}"
                           Label="{x:Bind Activity.TabLabel, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Hint="{x:Bind TabHint(Activity.OpensMore, Activity.HasPastLayers), Mode=OneWay}"
                           Clicked="OnTabClicked"/>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
